R"VG(
# news_sickness.vg (H-04's second pass): the news's register, continued: sickness and famine (moved here from news.vg as it grew), and the rite as
# a clause the items close on.

# ---- sickness and famine ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

news.sickness
  {news.h.sick}\n{news.sick.m} {news.sick.x}
  (medium=printed) {news.h.sick}\n{news.sick.m} {news.sick.x} {news.sick.t}
news.h.sick
  Sickness at {$e.place}
  {$e.sickness} spreads
  ($e.wave>1) {$e.sickness} returns
  Fever in the towns
  (age>=modern) Health warning
news.sick.m
  Cases of {$e.sickness} have been reported at {$e.place}; across the land the dead are now put at {#$e.value:about}.
  ($e.wave>1) {$e.sickness} has returned, first at {$e.place}, for the {#$e.wave:ord} time; the dead are put at {#$e.value:about}.
  The authorities at {$e.place} have closed the markets and the schools after an outbreak of {$e.sickness}.
  {$e.sickness} has reached {$e.place}, where [the doctors are working day and night|the hospital has turned the sick away|the doctors are fewer than the dead].
  (has:$e.place.quarter) The first deaths of {$e.sickness} at {$e.place} were in {$e.place.quarter}, and the street has been closed with ropes.
  An outbreak of {$e.sickness} at {$e.place} has killed {#$e.value:about} [since {season.now} began|in a month|in three weeks].
news.sick.x
  Travellers are advised to avoid the town, and the carriers have stopped taking parcels for it.
  (gov=monarchy) The palace has sent doctors and a cartload of [vinegar|lime|clean linen].
  (age>=industrial) The hospitals are said to be full, and {news.overflow} are taking the overflow.
  Residents are asked to boil their water, to stay indoors after dark and to keep the {herd} in.
  The {watersrc.n} at {$e.place} has been closed by order until the doctors have looked at it.
  The doctors blame [the water|the drains|the {pest}|the travellers|the heat], and the travellers blame the doctors.
  Funerals at {$e.place} are to be held at night and kept short, without {instrument}.
news.sick.t
  {news.said} that the worst is over, and the {colour.mourn} on the doors says otherwise.
  Prayers will be said at {holyplace} every evening until it passes, and {news.rite.n}.
  The {festival} fair at {$e.place} will not be held this year, nor the {ind.sport}.
  (age>=modern) A vaccine is said to be in trial, and the queue for it already reaches {town.open}.
  Those who can leave {$e.place} are leaving, with their {herd} and their {vessel}.
  The doctors of {$e.place} are burning {fuel} at the street corners, which the doctors of {city} call nonsense.

news.famine
  {news.h.famine}\n{news.famine.m} {news.famine.x}
  (medium=printed) {news.h.famine}\n{news.famine.m} {news.famine.x} {news.famine.t}
news.h.famine
  Hunger in the provinces
  (has:$e.place) Famine at {$e.place}
  Bread
  The hungry winter
news.famine.m
  The failure of the harvest has left many without bread; {#$e.value:about} are said to have died.
  Prices of {crop} have tripled since {season.now} began, and in the hill villages people are eating [the seed corn|the bark of the {tree.n}|the {herd}|whatever they can find].
  (has:$e.place) At {$e.place} the {crop} ran out before {season.now}; the dead there are put at {#$e.value:about}.
  There is no {crop} to be had in the markets of the south at any price, and {#$e.value:about} have died.
news.famine.x
  (gov=monarchy) The palace has opened the state granaries.
  (inv.railway=1) Relief trains have been sent with {food} and {crop}.
  Relief carts have been sent from the coast with salt fish and {fruit}.
  Bakers have been forbidden to raise their prices, and three of them have been fined for selling short.
  Soup is being given out in {town.open} at {$home} {time.of}, one bowl to a person.
  Hoarders will be [fined|named in this paper|sent to the mines], the council warns.
news.famine.t
  {news.said} that the next harvest looks better, and the {pest} disagree.
  The {festival} feast has been cancelled, and {feast.custom} with it.
  Emigration to the coast towns has doubled, and the {herd} go with the emigrants.
  This paper has opened a fund for the hungry; the first gifts, {n} {coin} and a {vessel.one.n} of {crop}, are listed on the back page.


# the rite as a clause after "and" ("and the fire will be kept")
news.rite.n
  (rite=firstfruits) the first of the {crop} will be given
  (rite=fire) the fire will be kept all night
  (rite=song) the old songs will be sung
  (rite=water) the water will be poured for {god}
  (rite=silence) the silence will be kept at noon
  (rite=fast) the fast will be kept
  (rite=pilgrimage) the faithful will go up to {holyplace}
  (rite=animals) the firstborn of the {herd} will be given
  (rite=memory) the names of the dead will be said
news.overflow
  the schools
  {holyplace}
  the {craft} works' sheds
  the inns
)VG"
